{"title":"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Dylan and Joey have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> costumes in total. Dylan gives Joey <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> costumes, and Joey now has the number of costumes that Dylan had before giving Joey any costumes. How many costumes does Dylan have now?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the initial number of costumes that Dylan had. This means that Joey had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/4/9b4d4c6f6feaa5c5de5a0ceff351e2924a865c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> at the start. When Dylan gave <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> costumes to Joey, Joey then had the same number of costumes that Dylan initially had. Thus, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f6c9211e1ea259aa27c634010ffe5f53f218afa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14 - x + 4 = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/0/660cab31d9c68c4de259c100e81b4a8af02e0c58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18 - x = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5e04e1c8bcf54e5c5c7c5ceec4f3df29f11fd7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/4865e10edcc1cf57f9e487f233516ce1f697ba0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{18}{2} = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"92\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Thus, Dylan had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50dc235165803ab9bf2f37b5607d87e61da8846a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 - 4 = \\boxed{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"87\" height=\"25\" /> costumes at the end.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of costumes that Dylan ended up with. This means that Dylan began with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5b4c3e97b90e7ed8f39e9634f062b3abc343052.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> costumes, and Joey had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/4/9b4d4c6f6feaa5c5de5a0ceff351e2924a865c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> costumes (since they have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> costumes in total and Dylan gave <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> costumes). Thus, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/24535bdec5c84a3d5d64ffc565cfc16bbd74447d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 4 = 14 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/3/9f3e14dfe956c1aa231216f1f3edac87e8bd82cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = 14 - 4 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4c093e97962894a6afe56562649262619be3ce4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{10}{2} = \\boxed{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018010858\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.067 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 82/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3217/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37870:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018010858 and revision id 292583. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}